welcome back to the david pakman show i  am farin cousins from ring of fire  sitting in for david pakman all of this  week  let's talk about january 6. shall we  obviously in the last few weeks here  we've gotten some  very important news i would call it  about the events of that day the events  before that day the powerpoints the text  messages the emails the phone calls  all kinds of stuff  but some of the most important  information we've gotten about january 6  has actually come from the courts  late last week  the harshest sentence to date for one of  the capitol rioters was handed down the  man who assaulted a police officer with  a fire extinguisher sentenced to a  little more than five years in prison  and of course this individual expressed  his uh  sorrow his sadness  at what he did you know  got the crocodile tears going um  but  judge didn't buy it  still sentence him to more than five  years  and this is  becoming routine at this point  this is what we're seeing happening  with these judges in the sentences that  they're handing down  and here's why and this is very  important and this is something that  everybody needs to understand  about the cases these judges are hearing  because judges are telling us this past  week  that january 6 is it's not over it's not  over  and the reason for that is because what  radicalized these individuals has not  stopped it has not gone away  while these particular people the the  ones who have been sentenced the ones  who are going to jail are currently in  jail they're probably not as likely to  engage in that kind of behavior in the  future  we're still creating another army  essentially  of these crazed people who think the  election was stolen  and that's what january 6 was  here's another thing  i filled in for david  back in august one of the stories i  talked about at the time i remember it  vividly  was the fact that judges back in august  were telling us  that we're probably facing another  january sixth type six uh situation  because of the radicalization process  because the big lie still persisted out  there  and in fact because it was being pushed  even harder in august than it was in  january  and now here we are four and a half  months after those judges told us that  more judges came out in the past week  and effectively told us the same thing  that we can expect more we can expect  worse  and we can expect this because the  radicalization still exists  because nothing has been done to stop it  because honestly it's hard to stop it  right these people have free speech we  can't tell them they're not allowed to  say these things that's illegal  but they're also not being held  accountable by the media outlets who  allow them to say these things  on their social media platforms where  they spew these lies every day in the  speeches that they give and again part  of this is because there's literally  nothing we can do about it all we can do  is go out there every day and talk about  how this is a lie this is not true all  of the evidence including the  uh audits and investigations conducted  by conservative groups are all telling  us there's no fraud there was no theft  but even still 70 percent of the  republican party believes joe biden is  not the dually elected president of the  united states  that the 2020 election was stolen 70  percent of republicans believe that now  and if we had listened to these judges  months ago  that wouldn't come as a shock  what happened on january 6th  was kind of an immediate radicalization  of individuals who were most of them  probably kind of already on the edge  they were hardcore supporters they had  their feelings hurt that their guy  didn't win  and then he told them go fight like hell  or you won't have a country anymore  hell one of the accused rioters last  week in in in front of a judge said  trump gave me permission to do this  i had a right to storm the capitol  because the former president gave me  permission  so they took that that one statement  from him and well the rest of it as well  that was their action and they went with  it  that's how quickly that radicalization  happened for many of those individuals  for the rest of them we're talking about  radicalization that's been going on for  a year now  radicalization that is taking hold  within the republican party to the point  70 percent look at joe biden and say  that man who i also think is incompetent  somehow stole the election  for the record two things can't be true  there he can't be such an incompetent  idiot you know he can't even stay awake  and a mastermind who stole the 2020  election that makes no sense  yet this is what they believe  and the judges are still out there  warning us that yeah things are going to  get bad again things are probably going  to be worse than what they already were  because nothing's being done  and in many instances there's nothing  legal we can do about it  all we can do is fight back against the  misinformation  and as somebody who does do this every  day and i'm sure david feels the same  way sometimes it feels like this  sisyphean task  we're pushing this boulder up the hill  only to watch it roll back down again  and start all over  there's no end there's no there's no  clear victory here  we're just destined to do this forever  to fight back against this conservative  misinformation  but like sisyphus himself we're never  going to stop  that's part of our job it's what we do  it's how we help  so that's what we're doing here  that's what these judges are trying to  do they're giving us the warnings  and if we don't heed these warnings  then yeah we're probably going to be  looking at something much worse than  what happened on january 6th at some  point  in the future
 

